      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63372,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Broad and other uterine ligaments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63373,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>The presentation is similar to that of uterine leiomyoma (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/237\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Uterine leiomyoma</em>) and these tumours often coexist with uterine leiomyoma. Massive ovarian oedema and pseudo&ndash;Meigs syndrome have been described {24901402; 9704185}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63374,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>The epidemiology is similar to that of uterine leiomyoma (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/237\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Uterine leiomyoma</em>).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:11:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63375,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/237\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Uterine leiomyoma</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:11:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63376,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours develop either from submesometrial smooth muscle layers, which run from the outer layer of the uterine myometrium to the pelvic floor, or from the round ligaments {17805565; 18661576; 21297441}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63377,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most are circumscribed, firm masses similar to their uterine counterparts. Some may exhibit prominent hydropic and degenerative cystic changes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63378,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The spectrum of histological changes encountered is the same as seen in leiomyomas from the uterus, including histological patterns such as leiomyoma with bizarre nuclei, leiomyoma with epithelioid morphology, and leiomyoma with lipomatous differentiation {14714722; 24414189; 19716558}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63379,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63380,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 206,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:41:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
